  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "5ThOsR5jRnZcCxOfw/vACrUCPYo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:39.249Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## What the preview actually is\n\nThe BUILD pane deep-links into the **reactor project** the agent spawned for the session \u2014 a dev-mode process, one per active build. The sequence: the agent calls `reactor-project-init` then `reactor-project-start` (both visible as tool cards), the dev server warms up in roughly 10\u201330 seconds, and the agent calls `spec-preview-show` with a project, drive and app reference to surface the app. From then on Vite HMR picks up generated code without a full reload.\n\nA running reactor project is **not sufficient on its own** \u2014 until the agent explicitly surfaces a preview the pane reads *\"No preview yet \u2014 The BUILD preview appears once the agent scaffolds a project for this session.\"*\n\n## Two things the preview cannot show you\n\n**Processors do not run.** They execute server-side in Switchboard, only once the studio is deployed. So any behaviour mediated by a processor \u2014 the doc's example is syncing a guest order to a staff board \u2014 looks broken in preview and starts working after deploy, with no code change in between. If you are debugging a missing read model or an unfired side effect in preview, the absence *is* the expected behaviour, not a bug to chase.\n\n**Preview drives are ephemeral and reset between sessions.** Documents you create to exercise the UI are not durable, so preview is not a place to build up test fixtures. This mirrors the local convention where the `vetra` drive holds source documents (models, editors, apps) and the preview drive holds instances \u2014 with the cloud preview drive additionally being disposable.\n\nBoth limits follow from the same fact: preview is a *dev render of the editors and apps*, not a runtime. Editors and drive apps are exactly the parts that live in the browser, so those are the parts you can see. Anything whose execution belongs to a host \u2014 processors, subgraph resolvers, sync channels \u2014 needs the real Switchboard.\n\nBecause the product is pre-alpha, the preview also does not always mount at all; if it stays on \"No preview yet\", deploy the app to see it end to end.\n\n_Source: `apps/academy/docs/academy/01-GetStarted/00-VetraStudio.md` (The BUILD preview), Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:37:38.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:39.249Z"
    }
  },
